    ("Zero FIR - Legal Rights in Crisis", "A 'Zero FIR' means you can walk into ANY police station in India to report a crime (especially sexual assault or harassment), regardless of where the crime took place. The police CANNOT refuse to file it citing jurisdiction. If an officer refuses, remind them of Section 166A of the IPC, which makes it a punishable offense for a police officer to refuse filing an FIR for serious offenses against women.", "Women"),
