    ("Surviving an Attempted Assault", "If physically attacked: 1) Do not hesitate. Strike primary vulnerable targets: Eyes (gouge or poke hard), Throat (strike the windpipe), Groin (knee or kick), and Instep (stomp hard on their foot). 2) Scream 'FIRE!' instead of 'Help!' (People are more likely to respond to fire). 3) Use anything as a weapon: keys protruding between fingers, a heavy bag, dirt/sand thrown in the eyes. 4) Your goal is not to win the fight, but to stun the attacker for 3 seconds to run away.", "Women"),
    ("Handling Cyber Stalking & Blackmail", "If someone is threatening to release private photos or doxing you: 1) DO NOT pay or negotiate. 2) Take screenshots of the threats, URLs, and profiles immediately. 3) Do not delete the chats; they are digital evidence. 4) Call the National Cyber Crime Helpline at 1930 or file a report at cybercrime.gov.in. Under Section 67A of the IT Act, publishing explicit material without consent is a non-bailable offense with up to 5 years in prison.", "Women"),
    ("Drink Spiking / Date Rape Drugs", "If you feel disproportionately intoxicated, dizzy, or lose coordination rapidly after a drink: 1) Tell a trusted friend immediately. Do not go to the bathroom alone. 2) If alone, go directly to the bartender or security staff and say 'I think I was drugged, call an ambulance.' 3) Do not accept a ride from a stranger or the person who bought the drink. 4) Seek medical attention immediately; drugs like GHB leave the system in hours, so rapid testing is essential for a police report.", "Women"),

