    ("Trapped in a Sinking Car", "If your car goes into the water: 1) Do NOT wait for the car to sink. You have roughly 30-60 seconds. 2) Unbuckle your seatbelt immediately. 3) DO NOT try to open the door (water pressure will prevent it). 4) Open the window immediately. If the power window fails, use a glass breaker tool, or remove the headrest and jam the metal pegs into the lower corner of the window to shatter it. 5) Swim out through the window.", "Disaster Survival"),
    ("Escaping a Building Fire", "In a major fire: 1) Get low. Toxic smoke kills long before flames do; crawl on your hands and knees where the air is cleanest. 2) Check doors with the back of your hand before opening. If hot, use another route. 3) If trapped in a room, stuff wet towels or clothing under the door crack. 4) Open a window slightly for air and hang a brightly colored cloth out the window to signal firefighters. Do not break the window, as you may need to close it if smoke enters from outside.", "Disaster Survival"),
    ("Surviving a Stampede / Crowd Crush", "If caught in a massive, crushing crowd: 1) Keep your arms up like a boxer (hands near your chest) to protect your ribcage and ensure you have space to expand your lungs. 2) Do not resist the force of the crowd; move with the flow, but work your way diagonally toward the edges. 3) Stay on your feet at all costs. 4) If you fall, curl into a fetal position, protect your head with your arms, and try to get up as quickly as humanly possible.", "Disaster Survival"),
